# Preserve list for the 0573f4c patch queue.
#
# Semantics: any upstream file listed here is **kept from the base**
# (src/upstream/0573f4c/) and produces **no patch**. The fork-side
# version under src/ — if any — is dropped in favour of the 0573f4c
# content. This applies to two distinct cases:
#
#   (a) Files NEW in the upstream base (not in src/): the upstream new
#       file is preserved by inheritance. No patch is needed because the
#       file already exists in the base.
#
#   (b) Files MODIFIED upstream AND present in src/ but WITHOUT a
#       fork-side delta: preserving the file keeps the upstream change
#       intact. Without preserving, the regen script would emit a modify
#       patch that effectively reverts the upstream change to baseline.
#
# Generated 2026-06-26 by carrying the b24b8cb preserve.list forward to
# the 0573f4c base. All 148 carried-over entries were verified present
# in src/upstream/0573f4c/. Section (h) adds the 87 files NEW in 0573f4c
# (upstream-only, absent from src/) so the new feature subsystems
# (workflow/, services/compact/, slash commands, bundled skills, new
# providers, query robustness, permission helpers) are inherited as
# base content with zero patch.
#
# CAVEAT: preserving a facade file (sections d/f/g) makes src/ take the
# 0573f4c base content, but the runtime still routes through the
# clawcodex_ext/ mirror, which currently sits on the OLD b24b8cb
# snapshot. The runtime feature gap is closed separately by 3-way
# merging 0573f4c into the clawcodex_ext mirrors. See
# CONFLICT_REPORT.md §2 / §3 for the per-file priority.

# (a) New in b24b8cb, no fork counterpart
